    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds a small, safe C++ wrapper around lexbor's HTML parser. This is **Phase 1** of the return-to-ADR-001 plan (see ADR-006) — it builds on Phase 0 (#91), which vendored lexbor as a submodule and proved it links.\n\nThe goal: future renderer code (layout, DOM, `window.cpp`) should never touch lexbor's raw C API directly. This wrapper is the only file in the project that includes lexbor headers.\n\n## What's Added\n\n- **`src/renderer/html/document.hpp`** — public interface\n- **`src/renderer/html/document.cpp`** — implementation (only file that includes lexbor)\n- **`tests/test_html_document.cpp`** — 7 test cases, 21 assertions\n- **`src/CMakeLists.txt`** — add `document.cpp` to `honeybee_lib`, link `lexbor_static` as `PRIVATE`\n- **`tests/CMakeLists.txt`** — register the new test file\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n| Decision | Rationale |\n|---|---|\n| **RAII wrapper** | `parse()` returns `unique_ptr<Document>`; destructor calls `lxb_html_document_destroy`. Callers never see a raw pointer. |\n| **Move-only, not copyable** | The underlying lexbor document has a single owner. Copying would create a use-after-free or double-free. |\n| **No exceptions** | Parse failure returns `nullptr`. Matches the style of `base/url.hpp` and `net/response.hpp`. |\n| **lexbor type forward-declared** | `struct lxb_html_document;` in the header means lexbor's C headers don't leak into every translation unit that includes `document.hpp`. |\n| **`lexbor_static` linked `PRIVATE`** | lexbor is an implementation detail of `honeybee_lib`. Tests link `lexbor_static` directly because they include the test body — that's fine, they're testing this integration. |\n\n## The Interface\n\n```cpp\nnamespace honeybee::renderer::html {\n\nclass Document {\npublic:\n    static std::unique_ptr<Document> parse(std::string_view html);\n    ~Document();\n\n    Document(Document&&) noexcept;\n    Document& operator=(Document&&) noexcept;\n    Document(const Document&) = delete;\n    Document& operator=(const Document&) = delete;\n\n    std::string title() const;\n    std::string text_content() const;\n\nprivate:\n    explicit Document(lxb_html_document* doc) noexcept;\n    lxb_html_document* doc_ = nullptr;\n};\n\n}\n```\n\n## Tests (21 assertions, 7 cases)\n\n1. Title extraction from `<title>Hi</title>`\n2. Missing `<title>` returns empty\n3. Malformed HTML (`<p>Unclosed`) parses gracefully\n4. Empty input parses to an empty document\n5. UTF-8 content preserved byte-for-byte (Arabic test string)\n6. Move-only semantics (source becomes `nullptr`, target owns)\n7. Nested text collected in document order (`<div><p>A</p><p>B</p></div>`)\n\n## Verification\n\n```\n$ cmake -S . -B build\n-- Lexbor version: 3.0.1\n-- Configuring done\n-- Generating done\n\n$ cmake --build build --target honeybee_tests\n[8/8] Linking CXX executable tests/honeybee_tests\n\n$ ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n1/1 Test #1: honeybee_tests ... Passed  5.09 sec\n100% tests passed, 0 tests failed out of 1\n\n$ ./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[document]\"\nAll tests passed (21 assertions in 7 test cases)\n```\n\n## Notes for the Reviewer\n\n- The wrapper's `title()` searches only the `<head>` subtree. That matches the WHATWG spec (title lives in head), and lexbor's parser guarantees only one `<title>` per document.\n- `text_content()` currently returns the concatenation of all text nodes **without whitespace normalization**. This is intentional for Phase 1 — whitespace handling is a layout concern and belongs in a later phase.\n- The `name_equals_ci` helper is a small case-insensitive comparison. It could be replaced by `lxb_dom_element_local_name` + `std::string_view` + `strncasecmp`, but a 10-line loop avoids a `#include <strings.h>` and works portably.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Builds locally\n- [x] All existing tests pass (including the Phase 0 smoke test)\n- [x] 7 new test cases, 21 assertions\n- [x] No GTK dependency added to `honeybee_lib`\n- [x] lexbor headers not leaked outside `document.cpp`\n\nCloses #92\n",
